<title>FRANCE: Socgen acts for Bouygues on Ciby.</title>
<headline>Socgen acts for Bouygues on Ciby.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>French bank Societe Generale confirmed on Monday that it had been hired by Bouygues to find a buyer for Bouygues' film production unit Ciby 2000.</p>
<p>&quot;I confirm that Bouygues has engaged us for this operation,&quot; a Societe Generale spokeswoman said in answer to Reuter questions.</p>
<p>Monday's issue of U.S. journal Daily Variety said that Bouygues had instructed Societe Generale and its American partner, investment bank Bannon &amp; Co, to find a buyer for Ciby 2000.</p>
<p>It said Bouygues hopes to raise $75 million from the sale of Ciby, which produced the films The Piano, Underground and Secrets and Lies.</p>
